    {
      "id": "AM4_Q6_X3",
      "difficulty": "X",
      "skill_tags": [
        "ratio_of_terms"
      ],
      "problem_text": "In (1+2x)^n, T_3 : T_2 = 7 : 1. Find n.",
      "answer": "n=7",
      "solution": "T_3=C(n,2)(2x)^2, T_2=C(n,1)(2x)^1. Ratio T_3/T_2=[C(n,2)4]/[C(n,1)2]=[n(n-1)/2 x 4]/[n x 2]=[2n(n-1)]/[2n]=(n-1)=7 => n=8. Wait: C(n,2)=n(n-1)/2. C(n,1)=n. So T_3/T_2=[n(n-1)/2 x 4x^2]/[n x 2x]=[2n(n-1)x^2]/[2nx]=(n-1)x=7. If x=1: n-1=7 => n=8",
      "marks": 3
